; Fish base as TWO sequential rabbit ears: triangle abd flattened at its
; incenter, then triangle cbd at its own — two independent single-vertex
; statements on opposite sides of the b-d line. Ear 1 is the CLASSIC fold in
; A′ even stated form (2026-07-18, owner ground truth): both halves of the
; diagonal given (`--ray & .a`/`--ray & .c`), no derive — the only mountain is
; the spine (the diagonal's continuation through the incenter), verified M=1 in
; the emitted assignments. The odd LineNew variant puts its mountain on a given
; bisector and is NOT the fish.
;
; Ear 2 is BLOCKED ON #48: after ear 1 commits the classic spine, the mark
; --l4 (map --bc onto --diag) reflects across the folded ear-1 joint and the
; current 2D fold-state cannot re-materialize it on the far flap —
; Fold_state.crease_segments returns [] and the flatten errors resolving --l4
; (task-51 report, Blocker B). The statement stays in the file so this case
; STARTS FAILING the moment the kernel rewrite lands and the error vanishes:
; flip it then to the full classic two-ear assertions (mountains only on the
; two spine emergents; derive the faces count from the folded state then).

paper square

mark --diag = map .a onto .c
mark --ray = through .a .c

step left
mark --l1 = map --ab onto --diag
mark --l2 = map --da onto --diag
flatten (--l1) (--l2) (--ray & .a) (--ray & .c) {toward .d}

step right
mark --l3 = map --cd onto --diag
mark --l4 = map --bc onto --diag
flatten (--l3) (--l4) (--ray & .c) (--ray & .a) {toward .d}

; expect error "--l4 has no material segment"
